        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Round box with cover of strung glass beads (called sablé) held together with looping stitches. Blue silk interior, pink silk base. White ground with blue and red balloon on top, with four oars extending from basket. Figure in basket and figure in left foreground. Design of balloon is that of Pierre Blanchard, first ascent 2 March 1784 (Paris). Good condition, touches of paint."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/ac927c6e-18bd-3307-a757-6b828e1c29cb> ;
